"""Shared candidate contact and material input findings."""
import json

def add_v25(d,P,new_page,para,table,picture):
 O=P/'engineering-v25-results'
 if not (O/'review_status.json').exists():return
 r=json.loads((O/'review_status.json').read_text())
 new_page(d,'V25 Checking a different surface calculation')
 para(d,'24 October 2026. Full software validation has not been achieved. We investigated one possible source of the changing joint stresses. The solid elements use quadratic interpolation, while the earlier contact calculation used smaller linear triangles on their faces. That approximation is not automatically wrong. We tested a quadratic surface alternative rather than assuming it was the cause.')
 para(d,'The candidate uses six node quadratic faces for both contact and applied surface loads. It matches the displacement interpolation on the solid boundary. Mathematical checks passed for shape functions, derivatives, triangle integration and projection. A random test field showed a difference from the old linear surface approximation; that number is a basis check, not a measured headphone error.')
 table(d,['New reference calculation','Relative force error'],[['Child large outward 1.9 mm target',format(r['cases'][0]['independent_residual'],'.2e')],['Child large outward 1.5 mm target',format(r['cases'][1]['independent_residual'],'.2e')],['Child large outward denser integration',format(r['quadrature_case']['independent_residual'],'.2e')]],[4.6,2.3])
 para(d,'All three solutions meet the same numerical consistency checks for equilibrium, independent residual, force, moment, friction, common rigid motion and contact derivatives. Raw solution fields, solver histories, source hashes and contact projection statistics are saved. A warm start only helps the solver begin; it still has to meet the final residual check.')
 para(d,'These remain isolated V19 joint calculations. The assumed stiffness is 3500 MPa, preload 140 N, friction 0.2 and outward force 2 N. The virtual spacer remains 0.5 mm. This is a change to the mathematical surface scheme, not a new CAD design, physical washer model or tested material.')
 new_page(d,'V25 The stress disagreement remains')
 picture(d,'V25_contact_comparison','The same finite stress sampling sets are compared. Five percent is our chosen comparison check, not a product safety standard.',6.55)
 para(d,str(r['mesh_passes'])+' of four mesh comparisons and '+str(r['quadrature_passes'])+' of four integration comparisons meet the chosen limit. The first comparison changes the target mesh from 1.9 to 1.5 mm. The second keeps the 1.9 mm mesh and increases integration from four to six Gauss points per axis. Both the 125 interior sample set and the 35 sample set including boundaries are retained.')
 para(d,'The quadratic surface method did not close reliable peak stress prediction. Better integration agreement cannot cancel a failed mesh check. Finite sampled peaks also do not bound the maximum everywhere in a part. We have kept the failed results and the original five percent limit.')
 para(d,'Because this candidate changes contact interpolation and consistent loading together, it does not prove which approximation caused earlier differences. We have not replaced the old model as a validated design or expanded this failed pilot into claimed adult and inward results. The actual edges, spacer, fastener, material condition and assembly loads still need to be represented.')
 new_page(d,'V25 Better inputs and the remaining work')
 para(d,'Manufacturer data help us choose realistic inputs, but a data sheet is not proof that our finished headphones work. BASF lists typical dry and conditioned tensile moduli of 3000 and 1100 MPa for uncoloured Ultramid A3K at 23 C. For an otherwise identical linear beam at the same deflection, that gives a stiffness and force ratio of about 0.37. This is a conditional calculation, not a prediction for our finished band. Our assumed 3500 MPa joint model is not calibrated to that grade or to humid conditions.')
 para(d,'The Rogers PORON 4701 40 product page lists a typical 25 percent compression value of 41 kPa for its 240 kg per cubic metre option. On an illustrative uniform 1000 square millimetre coupon that would be 41 N. That is not a real pad contact area or head force. We did not combine it with the different ISO global data sheet values or invent a complete foam curve from one point.')
 table(d,['Route or issue','What still needs to be defined'],[['SoftSpace joint','Actual spacer fastener edges loads and reliable stress prediction'],['SoftSpace worn cushion','Grade specific foam curves cover seams friction and head shapes'],['SoftSpace Flex Sony fit','Exact pad skirt groove carrier dimensions and tolerances'],['Both products sound and heat','Material and assembly inputs for calibrated seal acoustic and thermal models'],['Durability and folding','Completed assembly properties fatigue creep drop and continuous motion checks']],[2.25,4.65])
 para(d,'The Sony India replacement article we reviewed explains that methods vary by model and refers users to service. It supplies no mounting tolerances. This does not prove such dimensions are unavailable everywhere; the exact mounting fit remains unverified. Neither route gains a comfort, cooling, no leakage, ANC or sensory acceptance claim from this update.')
 para(d,'Sources checked on 24 October 2026: BASF Ultramid A3K product information September 2026; Rogers PORON 4701 40 product page and global standards sheet; Sony India article 00198705. Exact URLs, assumptions and calculations are saved in manufacturer_input_review.json. The remaining test register keeps failed, missing input and people dependent checks separate. Both products remain in development; neither has full software or physical sign off.')
